      "changes": [
        "Independently derive one numerical threshold N>=2, depending only on fixed theta>=0 and C>0, uniformly over every natural n>=N and every positive B<=C*n. At width n^(3/5), the source marginal-tail expression is bounded by n^(-100). Reuse Mathlib exponential-versus-real-power asymptotics and prove the uniform denominator estimate. This does not derive the geometric budget bound or the Hamiltonian tail estimate and introduces no new state or tail definition."
